    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on a favorable slate today, with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (71.52) anchoring the lineup against Chris Bassitt. Despite the right-on-right matchup, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** remains our highest-projected asset, buoyed significantly by a high-value park factor and his elite xwOBA metrics. He is closely followed by **Gunnar Henderson** (70.59); while his dynamic platoon split against Corbin technically drags his raw projection down, the park factor and his prime #2 slotting in the order keep him firmly in the \"Strong\" territory. **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) presents a high-upside play at 2B, benefiting from a soft matchup against Woods Richardson and a high-leverage leadoff opportunity that maximizes his potential to contribute to our scarcity-driven SB target.\n\nRounding out the active roster, **Coby Mayo** (65.57) and **Josh Jung** (61.01) provide reliable production. **Coby Mayo** is particularly interesting today; despite the LHP matchup against Corbin, the combination of a favorable park and consistent mid-order volume boosts his score well above his baseline. The most difficult decision in today's optimization was keeping **Miguel Vargas** (60.61) on the bench. **Miguel Vargas** cleared the \"Strong\" threshold comfortably, but his relative lack of power ceiling compared to the primary cohort left him as the odd man out in a crowded infield. We are keeping a close watch on the weather and official lineups, as any late shifts in park conditions could potentially flip the status of the bottom-tier starters, though currently, we are prioritizing the higher-floor efficiency of our active core.",
